==Enemy==
Alpacky has a slower attack rate than Camelle, but she's guaranteed to survive a lethal strike, and when her health reaches 1%, her damage multiplies by 10. Make sure that you either save a damage-dealing [[Cat Cannon]] for her lethal strike, use units with longer range than her, or with good timing, fast units will attack her before she can attack them.

==Strategy==
Despite her strengthen, the overall strategy for Alpacky is no different from what you would use against Camelle: use tanky melee units like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] to get real close and deal damage to her. Like how you would deal with an Assassin Bear, you can use your [[Cat Cannon]] for when she survives the lethal strike. However, if you are unlucky, the ability will activate before the lethal strike. If that happens, use units with good speed like [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]] to get the last few hits in.

[[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] such as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]] and [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]] can reach Alpacky through their Long Distance and hit her using peons as stepping stones. This is also true for [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]] and a few other alternatives, as waves and long distance attacks can consistently hit Alpacky. Additionally, waves are also a safe alternative to the Cat Cannon for her survive ability, as they can hit her while standing outside of her range.

